# Testing

## When Adding or Changing Code

1. **New code**: Write tests for all new code (components, hooks, utilities, API routes, pages). Place tests next to the code they cover (e.g. `__tests__/ComponentName.test.tsx` in the same directory or under `components/__tests__/`).
2. **Changed behavior**: Update existing tests that are affected by your changes so expectations match the new behavior.
3. **Before finishing**: Run the test suite and fix any failures. In `gospel-admin`, run `npm test` (or `npm test -- <name>` for a subset). Do not leave with failing or skipped tests unless there is an explicit, documented reason.

## Test Conventions (gospel-admin)

- Use **Jest** and **React Testing Library** for components and hooks.
- Mock external deps (e.g. `next/navigation`, `@capacitor/core`, Supabase) in tests so they are fast and deterministic.
- Prefer testing behavior and user-visible outcomes over implementation details.
- For new components/hooks, include at least: render (or mount), main user flows, and edge cases relevant to the feature.

## Commands

- `npm test` — run all tests
- `npm test -- <pattern>` — run tests matching the pattern (e.g. `CapacitorKeepLinksInApp`, `usePageTheme`)
- `npm run test:ci` — run tests in CI mode with coverage
